---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="wp-stage-sync — WordPress Staging Sync & Promote" description="Sync live WordPress to staging with smart WooCommerce filtering and anonymization, or promote themes and plugins from staging to live with automated backup and automatic restore." path="" current="home">
	<!-- HERO -->
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="hero-badge">
				<span class="hero-badge-dot"></span>
				Open Source · MIT License
			</div>
			<h1>Live-to-staging sync,<br><span>as easy as it should be.</span></h1>
			<p class="hero-sub">Sync live WordPress to staging with smart WooCommerce filtering and anonymization.
				Promote specific themes and plugins from staging to live with automated backup and automatic restore.
			</p>
			<div class="install-block">
				<span class="install-label">$ bash</span>
				<span class="install-cmd" id="heroCmd">curl -sSL https://ada.tools/wp-stage-sync/install.sh | bash</span>
				<button class="copy-btn" id="heroCopy" title="Copy command">
					<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
						<rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" />
						<path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 01-2-2V4a2 2 0 012-2h9a2 2 0 012 2v1" />
					</svg>
				</button>
			</div>
			<div class="trust-note" id="disclaimer">
				<p class="trust-note-text">
					<strong>Hey stranger.</strong> Don't trust anyone, and don't run random commands from the internet.
					Want to see what's inside the install script first?
					<a href="https://ada.tools/wp-stage-sync/install.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download it</a>
					and read it yourself. Or hand this prompt to your favorite AI agent and let it do the reading:
				</p>
				<div class="trust-prompt">
					<code class="trust-prompt-text"
						id="trustPrompt">Fetch https://ada.tools/wp-stage-sync/install.sh and review it line by line. Start your answer with a "TL;DR" section: one line stating whether it's SAFE or NOT SAFE to run, in plain language a non-technical person can understand. Then add a detailed breakdown for those who want it: explain every command, flag anything unexpected, dangerous, or outside the scope of installing a single binary, and call out anything that touches my filesystem or requires elevated privileges.</code>
					<button class="trust-copy" id="trustCopy" title="Copy prompt">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" />
							<path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 01-2-2V4a2 2 0 012-2h9a2 2 0 012 2v1" />
						</svg>
						<span>Copy prompt</span>
					</button>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="hero-ctas">
				<a href="https://github.com/AdaDigitalAgency/wp-stage-sync" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
					class="btn-primary">
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
						<path
							d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z" />
					</svg>
					View on GitHub
				</a>
				<a href="#how-it-works" class="btn-secondary">
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
						stroke-linecap="round">
						<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
						<polyline points="12 8 12 12 14 14" />
					</svg>
					How it works
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- SCREENSHOTS -->
	<section id="screenshots">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-label">Screenshots</div>
			<h2>See it in action.</h2>
			<p class="section-desc">Every step of the sync is guided by an interactive terminal interface.</p>
			<img src="images/screenshot-01.png" alt="WP Stage Sync — Welcome screen and directory selector"
				class="screenshots-hero-img" data-lightbox>
			<div class="screenshots-grid">
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-02.png" alt="Credential extraction">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Credential extraction</div>
				</div>
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-03.png" alt="Sync parameters">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Sync parameters</div>
				</div>
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-04.png" alt="Table sync modes">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Table sync modes</div>
				</div>
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-05.png" alt="Rsync excludes">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Rsync excludes</div>
				</div>
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-06.png" alt="Sync in progress">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Sync in progress</div>
				</div>
				<div class="screenshot-card" data-lightbox>
					<img src="images/screenshot-07.png" alt="Results">
					<div class="screenshot-card-label">Results</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- FEATURES -->
	<section id="features">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="features-header">
				<div class="section-label">Features</div>
				<h2>Everything you need,<br>nothing you don't.</h2>
				<p class="section-desc">Built for agencies managing multiple WordPress sites where a full-copy staging
					sync
					is risky, slow, or legally problematic.</p>
				<img src="images/wp-stage-sync.png" alt="wp-stage-sync logo" class="features-header-logo">
			</div>
			<div class="features-grid">
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" />
							<line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Smart Auto-Detection</h3>
					<p>Automatically discovers WordPress installs from Apache2, Nginx and LiteSpeed (Enterprise and OpenLiteSpeed) vhosts and filesystem paths.
						Parses <code
							style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px">wp-config.php</code>
						to extract credentials with zero manual setup.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<path d="M6 2L3 6v14a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2V6l-3-4z" />
							<line x1="3" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6" />
							<path d="M16 10a4 4 0 01-8 0" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>WooCommerce Order Filtering</h3>
					<p>Works with HPOS and legacy order storage. Exports only the N most recent (or oldest) orders — not your entire order history.
						Keeps customer accounts only for those included orders.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3" />
							<path d="M21 12c0 1.66-4 3-9 3s-9-1.34-9-3" />
							<path d="M3 5v14c0 1.66 4 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3V5" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Full WordPress Sync</h3>
					<p>No WooCommerce? It just works. Plain WordPress sites get a fast, complete copy of every
						table — no order filtering, nothing dropped.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 00-4-4H5a4 4 0 00-4 4v2" />
							<circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4" />
							<path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 00-3-3.87" />
							<path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 010 7.75" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Customer Anonymization</h3>
					<p>Optionally masks billing and shipping addresses, names, emails, and phone numbers in the staging
						database. Admin and editor accounts stay intact. Covers standard WooCommerce/WordPress fields —
						not a guarantee every plugin's PII is scrubbed.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>File Sync via rsync</h3>
					<p>Syncs <code
							style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px">wp-content/</code>
						with customizable folder exclusions. Detects staging webroot ownership and applies the correct
						<code
							style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px">chown</code>
						automatically.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
							<line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12" />
							<path
								d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 014 10 15.3 15.3 0 01-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 01-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 014-10z" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Domain Mapping</h3>
					<p>Runs WP-CLI search-replace for domain URLs. Handles Elementor URL settings
						automatically, puts Jetpack into safe mode, so your staging sites works out of the box.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Production Guardrails</h3>
					<p>The production database is strictly read-only — zero INSERT, UPDATE, or DROP, ever. Promote
						writes only the theme and plugin files you pick, always after a full backup with automatic
						restore.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="17 1 21 5 17 9" />
							<path d="M3 11V9a4 4 0 014-4h14" />
							<polyline points="7 23 3 19 7 15" />
							<path d="M21 13v2a4 4 0 01-4 4H3" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Promote & Restore</h3>
					<p>Surgically promote specific themes, plugins, and mu-plugins from staging to live. Automated
						tar.gz backup before each operation with automatic restore on failure.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<div class="feature-icon">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<path d="M1 12s4-8 11-8 11 8 11 8-4 8-11 8-11-8-11-8z" />
							<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<h3>Dry-Run Preview</h3>
					<p>Run with <code
							style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px">-n</code>
						to see exactly what a sync would export, transfer, and replace — every table, file, and command
						—
						without writing a single byte.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
	<section id="how-it-works">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-label">How it works</div>
			<h2>Four steps, fully automated.</h2>
			<p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 36px">Run <code
					style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px">wp-stage-sync</code>
				and the interface walks you through each phase.<br />After saving settings, use <code
					style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;background:var(--bg-subtle);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px">-u</code>
				for unattended runs. Use it in crons, in automations...</p>
			<div class="steps-wrap">
				<div class="step">
					<div class="step-num">Step 0</div>
					<h3>Database Export</h3>
					<p>Queries live DB read-only. Filters order tables in both order stores, excludes bulk session data.</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Target N orders from <code
								style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px">wc_orders</code> or <code
								style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px">wp_posts</code></li>
						<li>Linked customers preserved</li>
						<li>Structure-only export for specific tables</li>
						<li>Custom rules for order related tables</li>
					</ul>
					<div class="step-arrow">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6" />
						</svg>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="step">
					<div class="step-num">Step 1</div>
					<h3>Database Import</h3>
					<p>Drops all staging tables, imports clean with foreign key checks disabled.</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Full staging DB reset</li>
						<li><code
								style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px">FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS=0</code>
						</li>
						<li>Anonymization applied here</li>
					</ul>
					<div class="step-arrow">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6" />
						</svg>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="step">
					<div class="step-num">Step 2</div>
					<h3>File Sync</h3>
					<p>rsync with <code style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px">--delete</code>,
						skipping cache and build artifacts.</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Excludes top-level cache, ewww, litespeed, updraft etc.</li>
						<li>Toggle exclusions in interface</li>
						<li>Auto-detects ownership</li>
					</ul>
					<div class="step-arrow">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6" />
						</svg>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="step">
					<div class="step-num">Step 3</div>
					<h3>Post-processing</h3>
					<p>WP-CLI handles domain replacement and plugin-specific URL rewrites.</p>
					<ul>
						<li><code style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px">wp search-replace</code>
							all tables</li>
						<li>Elementor URL replace</li>
						<li>Jetpack safe mode</li>
						<li>Live CDN keys cleared on stage</li>
						<li>Stage caches of 16 cache plugins cleared, never live&rsquo;s</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- WOOCOMMERCE CALLOUT -->
	<section id="woocommerce">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="callout">
				<div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom: 10px">WooCommerce</div>
				<h3>HPOS or legacy order storage. Both are filtered.</h3>
				<p>With HPOS, wp-stage-sync reads the target orders from <code
						style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:rgba(0,115,170,0.08);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px">wc_orders</code>
					and filters every HPOS lookup table by order ID. With legacy storage, it reads them from <code
						style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:rgba(0,115,170,0.08);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px">wp_posts</code>
					and keeps only those orders and their meta. The order copies that HPOS compatibility mode keeps in
					<code style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:rgba(0,115,170,0.08);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px">wp_posts</code>
					are filtered too.</p>
				<div class="pill-row">
					<span class="pill">wc_orders</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_order_addresses</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_orders_meta</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_order_stats</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_order_product_lookup</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_order_tax_lookup</span>
					<span class="pill">wc_order_coupon_lookup</span>
					<span class="pill">wp_posts</span>
					<span class="pill">wp_postmeta</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- SAFETY -->
	<section id="safety">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-label">Safety</div>
			<h2>Production is safe.</h2>
			<p class="section-desc">The production database is enforced read-only at the query level. The default
				Live → Staging sync never writes to production at all; promote writes only the files you select,
				always after a backup.</p>
			<div class="safety-grid">
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Read-only live connection</h4>
						<p>Only SELECT and SHOW queries run against the production database — in both modes. Zero
							database writes, ever.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Path validation</h4>
						<p>Aborts if live and stage directories resolve to the same filesystem path (symlinks included).
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Database validation</h4>
						<p>Aborts if live and staging resolve to the same database — compared by server identity, not
							just the host string.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Backed-up promotes</h4>
						<p>Promote writes the files you select to live by design — after a full backup, with automatic
							restore on failure. The live database is never touched.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Live cache and CDN untouched</h4>
						<p>Staging gets live&rsquo;s Cloudflare, CDN and firewall keys cleared, and its own cache keys. A sync or a &ldquo;Purge All&rdquo; on staging never purges live&rsquo;s CDN or empties live&rsquo;s object cache.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="safety-item">
					<div class="safety-check">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
							stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
						</svg>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h4>Checks before any change</h4>
						<p>The sync stops before it touches staging if staging would share live&rsquo;s cache keys, or if a live setting it must clear cannot be read.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider">

	<!-- INSTALL -->
	<section id="install">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-label">Install</div>
			<h2>Up and running in seconds.</h2>
			<p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 36px">Requires Linux with MySQL/MariaDB, rsync, and WP-CLI
				available. Go 1.21+ only needed if building from source.</p>
			<div class="install-methods">
				<div class="install-card">
					<div class="install-card-header">
						<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--blue)"
							stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
							<polyline points="8 17 12 21 16 17" />
							<line x1="12" y1="12" x2="12" y2="21" />
							<path d="M20.88 18.09A5 5 0 0018 9h-1.26A8 8 0 103 16.29" />
						</svg>
						<h3>Quick Install</h3>
					</div>
					<div class="install-card-body">
						<div class="code-block">
							<button class="code-copy"
								data-copy="curl -sSL https://ada.tools/wp-stage-sync/install.sh | bash">
